{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1116435-memory-hole-why-no-withstand","id":1116435,"title":"Memory Hole - Why No Withstand?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-15T09:28:26-07:00","id":1116435,"title":"Memory Hole - Why No Withstand?","content":"I recently looked closer at the spells in the Mind arcanum, and I noticed the the spell &quot;Memory Hole&quot; hos no Withstand and I was wondering why this was.<br /> <br /> Is it an error or was it intentional for some reason?<br /> <br /> Basically all other spells that change the subject has a Withstand, so why is this the different?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T10:08:14-07:00","id":1116453,"title":"","content":"Because in 1e the default application of Memory Hole was to use it on yourself. Add a Withstand when using it offensively on someone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T13:56:47-07:00","id":1116546,"title":"","content":"So it is an error from Onyx Path.. Just wanted to ask to be sure that there wasn't a strange reason for this spell to allow removal of memories without any resistance..<br /> <br /> Also been wondering if it shouldn't cause Dissonance for sleepers to suddenly have your memory removed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T15:08:41-07:00","id":1116568,"title":"","content":"Depends on what memory is removed. Sometimes people forget what they're looking for when they step into a room, but most people don't lose several hours previously in the day. Can it be blamed on forgetfulness? Then it shouldn't cause Dissonance. Is it obvious amnesia? Then Dissonance should trigger once the subject realises something is amiss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T08:00:25-07:00","id":1117737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1116435-memory-hole-why-no-withstand?p=1116546#post1116546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it is an error from Onyx Path.. Just wanted to ask to be sure that there wasn't a strange reason for this spell to allow removal of memories without any resistance..<br /> <br /> Also been wondering if it shouldn't cause Dissonance for sleepers to suddenly have your memory removed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Memory holes don't seem magical to most people, even if they are unexplained. People will worry about drugs, illness, brain damage, mental trauma, and even blame simple stress for forgetting things. In general having a black-out is not seen as a metaphysical event.<br /> <br /> In real life at any moment your memory can fail, this happens to some people every day and everyone knows it is possible to happen to them at any time even if they push that knowledge to the very back of their mind and while that is frightening and disconcerting, it doesn't seem magical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-18-2017, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T01:49:12-07:00","id":1118447,"title":"","content":"That is true. But there are things that people normally wouldn't forget. Like if you got shot and don't know why.<br /> <br /> So I might make it a &quot;by case&quot; thing. Which I am kinda against as well, especially with something as &quot;wishy washy&quot; as this. It basically sais; &quot;the GM determines if it works or not&quot;. Which is OK, but to much uncertainty, in my experience, leads to inactivity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T02:43:05-07:00","id":1118461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1116435-memory-hole-why-no-withstand?p=1118447#post1118447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is true. But there are things that people normally wouldn't forget. Like if you got shot and don't know why.<br /> <br /> So I might make it a &amp;quot;by case&amp;quot; thing. Which I am kinda against as well, especially with something as &amp;quot;wishy washy&amp;quot; as this. It basically sais; &amp;quot;the GM determines if it works or not&amp;quot;. Which is OK, but to much uncertainty, in my experience, leads to inactivity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Determining whether a spell is obviously supernatural is always up to the ST regardless of spell. It's a huge improvement from 1E where specific spells always or never were obvious for sleepers regardless of whether it made sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T03:32:08-07:00","id":1118469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1116435-memory-hole-why-no-withstand?p=1118447#post1118447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is true. But there are things that people normally wouldn't forget. <b>Like if you got shot and don't know why.</b><br /> <br /> So I might make it a &quot;by case&quot; thing. Which I am kinda against as well, especially with something as &quot;wishy washy&quot; as this. It basically sais; &quot;the GM determines if it works or not&quot;. Which is OK, but to much uncertainty, in my experience, leads to inactivity.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sort of trauma is actually one of the most likely things to get naturally memory holed. If you read accounts by people who have survived life-threatening injuries, you will find that they often describe waking up in the hospital with no idea where they are or why their jaw is wired shut. Even long after the fact they often have at best confused snapshots of the event.<br /> <br /> On the other side of things people forget minor details all the time. Conversations we had, people we met, things we bought. It's not unusual to be unable to recall what you had for breakfast or where you put your car keys after coming home. And in most cases we don't even realize we forgot, because we'd have to remember to do that.<br /> <br /> So in my opinion, the most likely Memory Hole to cause Dissonance is if you cause them to forget something significant but non-traumatic that had witnesses. Like if they got a helicopter ride for their birthday and you made them forget, the mindfuckery of &quot;Hey you really liked that helicopter ride didn't you&quot; &quot;What? I've never been on a helicopter in my life.&quot; might be sufficient to cause Dissonance. Significant life events are also good candidates, but even forgetting your wedding day ten years ago is a pretty minor cause for concern compared to forgetting you went to a theme park yesterday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}